      "Language": "rum",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case is presented of intravascular hemolysis following incompatible transfusion of 500 ml hetero-group blood in a patient aged 29 years that had undergone emergency surgery for intra-abdominal hemorrhagic syndrome. Stress is laid on volemic therapy, on osmotic treatment and on the administration of alkalines in the first hours following the accident."},
